id: jf-0ea5
title: Ship OpenAPI-validated Jellyfin API execution
description: "Add a secure agent-first execution surface that resolves exact Jellyfin OpenAPI operations, validates methods paths parameters and bodies, defaults to read-only behavior, preserves all structured output formats, and strengthens executable API coverage evidence without replacing intuitive typed commands."
type: Plan
status: in_progress
priority: 0
tags[7]: agents,api,contracts,openapi,read-only,release,tool-schema
created_at: "2026-07-24T20:59:42.537Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-24T21:54:07.407Z"
assignee: codex-jellyfin-api
author: codex-jellyfin-api
estimated_minutes: 600
acceptance_criteria: Exact operation IDs and METHOD/path pairs resolve deterministically against the configured server OpenAPI document; GET HEAD and OPTIONS execution is permitted by default while mutating methods require explicit opt-in and remain blocked by global read-only mode; Query path and JSON body inputs are parsed and validated without forwarding credentials outside the configured origin; TOON JSON YAML Markdown table and raw output remain valid and agent tool schemas fully describe the new interface; Help docs setup validation unit integration package and live compiled read-only acceptance are green with no private data committed
goal: jf-mqpo
value: Give humans and agents complete forward-compatible Jellyfin API reach with exact contract evidence.
impact: Eliminates the gap between fuzzy coverage claims and executable operation access while keeping private auth and mutation safety boundaries.
outcome: "Every live OpenAPI operation can be resolved and safely invoked through a structured CLI contract, with read-only acceptance and honest quality evidence."
why_now: "The live mapper reports 100 percent semantic coverage, but prior PM evidence correctly says that is insufficient to claim complete implementation."
parent: jf-gn5j
reviewer: github-review-bots
risk: high
confidence: high
sprint: jellyfin-10.11.11
release: next-manual-release
