comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T21:00:03.345Z",codex-jellyfin-api,"Repository memory, all 40 PM items, active metadata, graph lineage, current GitHub state, official Jellyfin sources, and sanitized live 10.11.11 schema/readiness results were reviewed before implementation. No duplicate API-delivery item was found."
  "2026-07-24T21:40:17.869Z",codex-jellyfin-api,"Release evidence is green for the delivered API surface. Repository-wide 100% four-metric coverage and zero duplication are not yet true: 38.65/38.31/50.27/38.32 and 8.63% respectively. These pre-existing gaps remain open under canonical related items jf-mkzh and jf-lpki; this work neither lowers nor excludes any threshold."
  "2026-07-24T21:53:03.901Z",codex-jellyfin-api,"PM linked-test execution proved 13/13 focused and 179/179 compiled live tests. Its release command alone produced a false changelog mismatch because tracker sandboxing detached Git release-tag context despite exact 41-item parity. Direct validate:release remains green. Detailed duplicate search found no matching pm-cli report, so core issue unbraind/pm-cli#682 records the distinct source-workspace identity defect; related #678 is extension discovery, not this behavior."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T21:00:04.295Z",codex-jellyfin-api,"Privacy boundary: raw live schema/research stays under ~/.jellyfin-cli with 0700/0600 permissions; PM, git, logs, and PR evidence may contain counts/version/contract shape only, never server URL, credentials, entity IDs, library inventories, or raw payloads."
  "2026-07-24T21:40:19.162Z",codex-jellyfin-api,Private Jellyfin credentials and raw OpenAPI/live response material remain only under owner-only ~/.jellyfin-cli. Git-tracked documentation contains sanitized version and aggregate operation counts only. Every live command used JELLYFIN_READ_ONLY=1; mutation behavior was exercised exclusively against an isolated loopback Bun server.
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T21:43:39.568Z",codex-jellyfin-api,Local tarball smoke tests must use a fresh Bun install cache per packed artifact. Reusing Bun cache state for the same unreleased package version can produce an integrity mismatch even when npm pack is valid; scripts/smoke-bunx.mjs now isolates both package and cache directories.
